+## Source intelligence
+
+For Windows, the portable installer at `deploy/intelligence/Install-Windows.cmd`
+copies the bundled Skill to `%USERPROFILE%\.agents\skills\last30days`, with an
+automatic backup of an existing copy. Its package includes the official `tzdata`
+IANA data because Windows normally has no system zoneinfo database. Running a
+source checkout on Windows instead requires installing `tzdata` for the selected
+Python interpreter. Neither installation enables scheduling or actual delivery.
+
+Primary use is `/last30days intelligence discover AI systems`, `trace <retrieved-url>`,
+`explore <retrieved-url>`, `watch add/list/run`, or `briefing daily/weekly`. The Skill
+routes this before ordinary first-run/browser/key prompts. It uses a dedicated
+stdlib-only Python 3.12+ entry and preserves ordinary research and trending routes.
+The [Chinese operator guide](docs/source-intelligence.md) covers installation,
+schedulers, Webhook/Telegram/Feishu setup, and verification limits.
+
+Copy the [non-secret JSON defaults](skills/last30days/intelligence.example.json)
+and [private environment template](skills/last30days/intelligence.env.example)
+outside the repository. Store real endpoints, bot tokens, chat IDs and SMTP
+credentials only in process environment or an explicit private `--env-file`;
+protect that file with mode `0600`. The CLI uses the upstream `load_env_file`
+reader as data and fills only unset environment variables. Never shell-source
+it. JSON rejects unknown settings and is not a credential store.
+
+For dedicated CLI/fallback/cron use, global options precede the operation:
+
+```bash
+python3 skills/last30days/scripts/intelligence.py \
+  --config ~/.config/last30days/intelligence.json \
+  --env-file ~/.config/last30days/intelligence.env discover "AI systems"
+
+python3 skills/last30days/scripts/intelligence.py \
+  --config ~/.config/last30days/intelligence.json \
+  --env-file ~/.config/last30days/intelligence.env deliver
+```
+
+`--send` is explicit actual delivery; without it, preview queued cards. Adding a
+watch persists a due job but does not install cron/systemd. Scheduling examples
+default to preview and are never activated by installation of this Skill.
+
+| Path/control | Precedence or behavior |
+|---|---|
+| JSON settings file | `--config` > `LAST30DAYS_INTEL_CONFIG` > existing `~/.config/last30days/intelligence.json` > built-in defaults; no project-file auto-loading |
+| SQLite path | `--db` > process `LAST30DAYS_INTEL_DB` > explicit env-file value > JSON `db` > `~/.local/share/last30days/research.db` |
+| Local reports | `--report-dir` > process `LAST30DAYS_INTEL_REPORT_DIR` > explicit env-file value > JSON `report_dir` > `~/.local/share/last30days/intelligence/reports` |
+| Enabled channels | `LAST30DAYS_INTEL_CHANNELS`, comma-separated names; process environment overrides env-file |
+| JSON `channels` | Optional allow-list intersecting enabled environment channels; `[]` means no additional restriction, not implicit sending |
+| JSON timezone | `Asia/Shanghai` by default; any installed IANA timezone; defines complete daily/ISO-week briefing windows |
+
+`~` expands in paths; `$HOME` text in JSON/dotenv is not shell-expanded. Ordinary
+`LAST30DAYS_MEMORY_DIR` and `LAST30DAYS_STORE` retain their original meanings; the
+intelligence route writes its own reports/history without requiring `--store`.
+It adds `intel_*` tables while preserving the upstream SQLite schema version.
+
+JSON controls and defaults:
+
+| Setting | Default | Scope |
+|---|---|---|
+| `limits.max_depth`, `max_calls`, `max_nodes` | `2`, `30`, `25` | Observed relationship depth, bounded operations, graph nodes |
+| `limits.max_seconds`, `request_timeout`, `max_bytes` | `180`, `12`, `1048576` | Run deadline, public-source request seconds, per-resource bytes |
+| `limits.max_cost_usd` | `0` | Paid API budget; MVP discovery stays free-only even when paid credentials exist |
+| `lookback_days`, `max_reports` | `30`, `4` | Discovery window and reports per scan |
+| `engine_sources` | `["reddit", "hackernews"]` | Explicit free upstream sources; optional X requires pinned `bird` and authorized manual cookies, never browser extraction |
+| `cache_seconds`, `source_check_interval_seconds` | `86400`, `3600` | Cached snapshot age and accumulated-source recheck cadence |
+| `local_proxy_url` | `null` | Explicit unauthenticated loopback HTTP proxy for known public providers on an unmanaged Fake-IP network |
+| `threshold_a`, `threshold_b`, `confidence_threshold` | `65`, `60`, `0.7` | A/B value proxies plus primary-evidence eligibility; new A alerts also require the completed six-field Agent review; evidence-poor observations stay `hold` |
+| `min_delivery_interval_seconds` | `1` | Per-channel interval persisted in SQLite; flush defers rather than sleeping |
+| `weights` | novelty `.15`, originality `.15`, technical value `.20`, application potential `.15`, confidence `.20`, evidence quality `.15`, engagement `0` | Configurable deterministic proxies; weighted score does not establish scientific innovation |
+
+For interactive discovery, the Skill's routed reference requires the host Agent
+to generate purposeful query directions, collect upstream clues with `--collect-only
+--plan --native-search`, use available native search/read tools, compare resources,
+then trace selected snapshots with `--seeds --host-observations --host-only --analyses`.
+Without native search, the original bounded primary adapters remain available. The plan is
+bounded trusted local JSON (`last30days-intelligence-plan/1`, matching `domain`,
+1–6 distinct `queries` containing `query`, `rationale` and optional `providers`
+with github/arxiv/web query strings). `--plan` and `--seeds`
+are mutually exclusive; collection-only cannot send or queue cards. The CLI
+labels resource-shape triage as semantically unreviewed and fairly shares one
+tracing budget across selected candidates. Bare `discover` remains available
+for headless deterministic discovery. The run's `research_handoff` makes pending
+native searches and sparse candidate pools explicit. The host expands sparse
+directions, aiming for about 12 plausible resources before selecting 2–3 findings;
+the target is not a claim of exhaustive coverage or permission to pad results.
+Default interactive exploration limits are 10 minutes/40 external search/read attempts;
+the host records actual retrieval, local snapshot processing and total wall time
+separately, while each CLI invocation also enforces its own processing/node/time limits.
+
+`--analysis` accepts an optional six-field `assessment`: `finding`, `new`,
+`why_it_matters`, `application_potential`, `limitations`, `next_steps`. Each field
+contains `text` plus `evidence` references with an available snapshot URL and an
+exact 20–1000 character quote. This updates report prose as AI interpretation;
+it does not award points or assert independent verification. Existing `insights`
+remain supported. The evidence-value/2 proxies exclude unrelated dependencies,
+metadata-only pages and background profiles from technical value. New-to-store
+is not scientific novelty; legacy inflated scores are recomputed on a revisit.
+`discover --analyses` accepts a bounded (256 KiB) object mapping selected resource
+URLs to these analysis objects. `briefing research --domain <domain> --event-id
+<stored-id>` uses cached current revisions, preserves the Agent's chosen order and
+writes a Chinese JSON/Markdown brief without network retrieval, queues or sends.
+Cron does not implicitly run an LLM: without host review, analysis is labeled
+`agent_review_required`.
+
+The default A threshold is 65 for evidence-value/2. A supported single-primary
+dated/versioned material-update path can reach 66.75 with default weights; the
+old 85 (and the intermediate 75) cannot. Explicit private thresholds are kept,
+including 85; revise that setting if you want A eligibility under these proxies.
+This calibrates observable evidence signals, not a higher innovation claim.
+Same-revision validated analysis is retained on rechecks and in period digests.
+Never-attempted pending A payloads can adopt the reviewed text without creating
+another alert; attempted or acknowledged payloads remain immutable.
+
+If an already authorized native/MCP tool retrieved public documents, an explicit
+`--host-observations` file can import actual bodies and provenance. Its schema is
+`last30days-host-observations/1`; up to 25 observations each contain only `url`,
+`text`, `content_type`, `tool`, `retrieved_at` (timezone-aware). The file limit is
+5 MiB and each text is at most 1 MiB. Quotes/hash/time are retained, HTTP status
+is unknown, and transport/DNS/TLS verification is host-reported rather than
+claimed as CLI HTTP. The file must be created from real tool responses, never
+invented source content. With `--host-only`, missing material is recorded as
+`host_material_required` for a host reader; no anonymous fallback occurs. Without
+that explicit flag, missing resources use the ordinary resolver. Maintain
+a separate aggregate ledger for host calls and multiple CLI invocations; each
+CLI hard budget covers only its own run.
+
+The upstream discovery subprocess is one coarse budget operation with a hard
+deadline. Internal upstream HTTP calls are not individually counted; primary
+adapter/traversal operations are separately bounded. Free retrieval does not
+promise unrestricted access: 403/429/auth and network-policy failures stay in
+source outcomes rather than becoming fabricated quiet-domain conclusions. Typed
+HTTP quota hints preserve rate-limit remaining/reset/resource and numeric Retry-After,
+without arbitrary response bodies, cookies or headers. A 403 without rate-limit
+evidence remains an unknown access denial; it is not automatically an auth failure.
+
+Clash/Mihomo Fake-IP DNS can resolve public GitHub names into the reserved
+`198.18.0.0/15` range, which ordinary address validation correctly rejects.
+On a user-controlled unmanaged machine, set `local_proxy_url` in the private
+JSON to `http://127.0.0.1:<mixed-or-HTTP-port>` (or numeric `[::1]`). The port
+must be explicit; SOCKS, authentication, remote proxies and URL paths are
+rejected. This delegates DNS only for the exact known provider hosts in
+`transport.py`; unknown websites still require checked public addresses.
+HTTPS CONNECT and origin certificate verification remain enabled. Retrieval
+metadata reports `delegated_to_trusted_local_proxy` and
+`local_address_verified: false`; the proxy endpoint is not saved in evidence.
+The configured proxy is a local trust boundary, not proof of its remote DNS
+address. A managed environment policy takes precedence and cannot be overridden.
+Use `deploy/intelligence/Repair-Clash.cmd` from the dedicated repair ZIP after
+installing the Windows bundle. It backs up supported installed files, probes
+real GitHub HTTPS before saving opt-in, then runs a bounded trace without sends.
+It does not edit Clash settings or the Windows system proxy.
+
+Channel variables (all names below use the `LAST30DAYS_INTEL_` prefix):
+
+| Channel name | Required suffixes | Optional suffixes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `webhook` | `WEBHOOK_URL` (HTTPS) | `WEBHOOK_TOKEN` (Bearer) |
+| `telegram` | `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` | none |
+| `feishu` | `FEISHU_WEBHOOK_URL` (HTTPS) | `FEISHU_SECRET` (custom-bot signing secret) |
+| `slack` | `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` (HTTPS) | none |
+| `wecom` | `WECOM_WEBHOOK_URL` (HTTPS) | none |
+| `smtp` | `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_FROM`, `SMTP_TO` (comma-separated) | `SMTP_PORT` (465 for ssl, 587 for starttls), `SMTP_TLS` (`ssl` or `starttls`), paired `SMTP_USERNAME`/`SMTP_PASSWORD` |
+
+Generic Webhook is the recommended first destination. All adapters retain
+primary-source links, quotations, verification status, uncertainty and score
+context. The outbox deduplicates event/revision/channel/tier/period, persists
+acknowledged chunks, uses expiring atomic leases, and retries due failures with
+exponential backoff (3 attempts per chunk by default). The generic payload and
+`Idempotency-Key` header carry a stable per-chunk key for receiver deduplication.
+Remote acknowledgment loss can repeat a send: delivery is at-least-once.
+
+HTTP uses inherited proxies and verified TLS and rejects redirects; no proxy or
+certificate bypass is used. SMTP uses verified implicit TLS or STARTTLS socket
+transport, and HTTP proxy variables do not configure an SMTP relay. Errors/config
+repr and persisted delivery state exclude credentials/secret destination URLs.
+Local report paths are private file pointers, not usable remote URLs; hosted
+report publication is not implemented by this route.
+
+---
+
